The Purge: Anarchy is a 2014 American action horror film
written and directed by James DeMonaco.

12
00:56:10,909 --> 00:56:16,909
A sequel to  The Purge and the second installment in the Purge franchise, the film stars
Frank Grillo, Carmen Ejogo, Zach Gilford, Kiele Sanchez, and Michael K.

13
01:00:51,818 --> 01:00:57,818
Edwin Hodge reprised his role from the first film.

14
01:05:32,727 --> 01:05:38,727
It was released worldwide on July 18, 2014.

15
01:10:13,636 --> 01:10:19,636
The film is set in a near-future dystopian United States, ruled by a totalitarian government known as the New Founding Fathers of
America (NFFA), that is preparing for the annual Purge, a 12-hour event that legalizes all crimes without authorities.

16
01:14:54,545 --> 01:15:00,545
However, an anti-Purge resistance group opposes the NFFA and the Purge.

17
01:19:35,454 --> 01:19:41,454
The film grossed over $111 million and received mixed reviews from critics, who praised it as an
improvement over its predecessor, but criticized its clichéd formula and screenplay.

18
01:24:16,363 --> 01:24:22,363
While the first film was set largely in one house, Anarchy takes place around the Greater Los
Angeles area and shows more of what happens to the surroundings during the event.

19
01:28:57,272 --> 01:29:03,272
A third film in the series, The Purge: Election
Year, was released on July 1, 2016.

20
01:33:38,181 --> 01:33:44,181
The film explores themes of sniper, psychopath, bus, assault rifle, dystopia.

21
